></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">C</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-plus-3-t1-l-q21\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"C\"></span><span>she had been inspired by a particular book.</span></div></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"><span><strong class=\"source-question-number\">22</strong> Phoebe's main research question related to</span><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">A</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-plus-3-t1-l-q22\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"A\"></span><span>the effect of teacher discipline.</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">B</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-plus-3-t1-l-q22\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"B\"></span><span>the variety of learning activities.</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">C</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-plus-3-t1-l-q22\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"C\"></span><span>levels of pupil confidence.</span></div></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"><span><strong class=\"source-question-number\">23</strong> Phoebe was most surprised by her finding that</span><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">A</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-plus-3-t1-l-q23\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"A\"></span><span>gender did not influence behaviour significantly.</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">B</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-plus-3-t1-l-q23\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"B\"></span><span>girls were more negative about school than boys.</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">C</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-plus-3-t1-l-q23\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"C\"></span><span>boys were more talkative than girls in class.</span></div></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"><span><strong class=\"source-question-number\">24</strong> Regarding teaching, Phoebe says she has learned that</span><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">A</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-plus-3-t1-l-q24\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"A\"></span><span>teachers should be flexible in their lesson planning.</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">B</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-plus-3-t1-l-q24\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"B\"></span><span>brighter children learn from supporting weaker ones.</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">C</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-plus-3-t1-l-q24\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"C\"></span><span>children vary from each other in unpredictable ways.</span></div></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"><span><strong class=\"source-question-number\">25</strong> Tony is particularly impressed by Phoebe's ability to</span><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">A</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-plus-3-t1-l-q25\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"A\"></span><span>recognise the limitations of such small-scale research.</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">B</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-plus-3-t1-l-q25\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"B\"></span><span>reflect on her own research experience in an interesting way.</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">C</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-plus-3-t1-l-q25\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"C\"></span><span>design her research in such a way as to minimise difficulties.</span></div></div></div>","sourceQuestionCount":5},{"id":"en-plus-3-t1-l-g3-1","type":"source_html","ieltsQuestionType":"matching_features","instructions":"","sourceHeading":"Questions 26-30","sourceHtml":"<div class=\"source-question-section-content\"><p>What did Phoebe find difficult about the different research techniques she used?</p><p>Choose FIVE answers from the box and write the correct letter A-G.</p></div><div class=\"source-questions\"><div class=\"matching-dnd-questions\"><div class=\"source-question-item\"> • Observing lessons<span class=\"options-drop-zone dnd-zone\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">26</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-plus-3-t1-l-q26\" data-luma-kind=\"drop\"></span></span></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"> • Interviewing teachers<span class=\"options-drop-zone dnd-zone\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">27</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-plus-3-t1-l-q27\" data-luma-kind=\"drop\"></span></span></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"> • Interviewing pupils<span class=\"options-drop-zone dnd-zone\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">28</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-plus-3-t1-l-q28\" data-luma-kind=\"drop\"></span></span></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"> • Using questionnaires<span class=\"options-drop-zone dnd-zone\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">29</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-plus-3-t1-l-q29\" data-luma-kind=\"drop\"></span></span></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"> • Taking photographs<span class=\"options-drop-zone dnd-zone\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">30</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-plus-3-t1-l-q30\" data-luma-kind=\"drop\"></span></span></div></div><div class=\"options-dnd-panel dnd-panel dnd-panel--matching\"><div class=\"dnd-panel-instruction\">Drag and drop an option to fill in each blank.</div><div class=\"dnd-cards-container\"><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"A\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">A.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">Obtaining permission</span></div><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"B\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">B.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">Deciding on a suitable focus</span></div><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"C\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">C.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">Concentrating while gathering data</span></div><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"D\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">D.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">Working collaboratively</span></div><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"E\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">E.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">Processing data she had gathered</span></div><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"F\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">F.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">Finding a suitable time to conduct the research</span></div><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"G\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">G.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">Getting hold of suitable equipment</span></div></div></div></div>","sourceQuestionCount":5}],"audio_fallbacks":["https://engnovate.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/practice_test_plus_3_academic_listening_test_1_3.mp3"],"order_index":3},{"id":"en-plus-3-t1-l-p4","title":"Part 4","part_number":4,"passage_text":"","audio_url":"https://ielts-listening-audio.engnovatemedia.com/3127761-practice_test_plus_3_academic_listening_test_1_4.mp3","question_groups":[{"id":"en-plus-3-t1-l-g4-0","type":"source_html","ieltsQuestionType":"diagram_labelling","instructions":"","sourceHeading":"Questions 31-40","sourceHtml":"<div class=\"source-question-section-content\"><div class=\"source-section-content-wrapper\"><p>Complete the sentences below.</p><p>Write NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS for each answer.</p><p><b>Saving the juniper plant</b></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><b>Background</b></p><p>Juniper was one of the first plants to colonise Britain after the last <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">31</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-plus-3-t1-l-q31\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>.</p><p>Its smoke is virtually <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">32</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-plus-3-t1-l-q32\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> , so juniper wood was used as fuel in illegal activities.</p><p>Oils from the plant were used to prevent <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">33</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-plus-3-t1-l-q33\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> spreading.</p><p>Nowadays, its berries are widely used to <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">34</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-plus-3-t1-l-q34\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> food and drink.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><b>Ecology</b></p><p>Juniper plants also support several species of insects and <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">35</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-plus-3-t1-l-q35\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><b>Problems</b></p><p>In current juniper populations, ratios of the <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">36</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-plus-3-t1-l-q36\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> are poor.</p><p>Many of the bushes in each group are of the same age so <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">37</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-plus-3-t1-l-q37\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> of whole populations is rapid.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><b>Solutions</b></p><p>Plantlife is trialling novel techniques across <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">38</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-plus-3-t1-l-q38\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> areas of England.</p><p>One measure is to introduce <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">39</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-plus-3-t1-l-q39\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> for seedlings.</p><p>A further step is to plant <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">40</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-plus-3-t1-l-q40\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> from healthy bushes.</p></div></div><div class=\"source-questions\"><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div></div>","sourceQuestionCount":10}],"audio_fallbacks":["https://engnovate.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/practice_test_plus_3_academic_listening_test_1_4.mp3"],"order_index":4}],"questions":[{"id":"en-plus-3-t1-l-q1","part_id":"en-plus-3-t1-l-p1","group_id":"en-plus-3-t1-l-g1-0","question_type":"source_text","ieltsQuestionType":"note_completion","question_text":"","correct_answer":"an accountant/accountant","correct_answer_variants":["an accountant","accountant"],"answerCount":1,"sourceNumbers":[1],"sourceInputName":"ielts_listening_answer_3127686_1","order_index":1,"points":1},{"id":"en-plus-3-t1-l-q2","part_id":"en-plus-3-t1-l-p1","group_id":"en-plus-3-t1-l-g1-0","question_type":"source_text","ieltsQuestionType":"note_completion","question_text":"","correct_answer":"over 50/over fifty","correct_answer_variants":["over 50","over fifty"],"answerCount":1,"sourceNumbers":[2],"sourceInputName":"ielts_listening_answer_3127686_2","order_index":2,"points":1},{"id":"en-plus-3-t1-l-q3","part_id":"en-plus-3-t1-l-p1","group_id":"en-plus-3-t1-l-g1-0","question_type":"source_text","ieltsQuestionType":"note_completion","question_text":"","correct_answer":"family membership/family","correct_answer_variants":["family membership","family"],"answerCount":1,"sourceNumbers":[3],"sourceInputName":"ielts_listening_answer_3127686_3","order_index":3,"points":1},{"id":"en-plus-3-t1-l-q4","part_id":"en-plus-3-t1-l-p